Digitalis prebuilts, redistributed with Prism so the ARM64 translator does not have to be built
from AOSP source. This copy comes from the Refract project's bundle (see MANIFEST.txt), which
includes Refract's performance changes to system/lib64/libberberis_arm64.so.

Digitalis / Berberis (system/lib64/libberberis_*, system/bin/berberis_program_runner_*,
system/etc/*): Apache License 2.0. Digitalis: https://github.com/DigitalisX64. Berberis is part
of the Android Open Source Project:
https://android.googlesource.com/platform/frameworks/libs/binary_translation/

arm64 guest libraries (system/lib64/arm64/*, system/bin/arm64/*): built from the Android Open
Source Project. Each keeps its upstream license: mostly Apache License 2.0; bionic (libc, libm,
libdl, linker) BSD-style; ICU (libicu*) Unicode License; BoringSSL (libcrypto, libssl)
OpenSSL/ISC; zlib (libz) zlib License; SQLite (libsqlite) public domain; libc++ Apache 2.0 with
LLVM exception. Full texts are in the AOSP source tree (https://source.android.com/), under each
project's LICENSE or NOTICE file.

Prism does not modify these files in the repository. At build time, tools/translator.py makes
copies whose DT_NEEDED entry for libc++.so points at Prism's compatibility shim instead (see
native/berberis_compat), so the Android 16 build loads on Android 14.

